WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.412
Now read the findings, and each
rule shows up in a realistic shape.

2
00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:09.024
A mail automation app holds the broad
directory permission with no exception.

3
00:00:09.024 --> 00:00:12.188
A connector's exception
quietly ended last month.

4
00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:14.746
A mail permission is "scoped" in Exchange,

5
00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:18.776
but the unscoped grant is still
there, so the scope does nothing.

6
00:00:18.776 --> 00:00:21.269
A batch machine's managed
identity holds roles

7
00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:23.700
at the subscription and
the management group.

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.175
Three apps can grant themselves
more, so they're handed off.

9
00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:30.920
And in the review, one answer
from July doesn't count any more,

10
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.590
because it's a new quarter.
